rrors.New(\"gitx: transient remote or network failure\")`. New.\n.ard/357/plan.md:7:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/357/plan.md:8:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/357/plan.md:9:4. `internal/gitx/local.go` `classifyFetch`: return `ErrTransient` for the same stderr patterns after the existing `ErrRefNotFound`/`ErrRepoAccess` checks (those win). Do not treat a 403/404 as transient.\n.ard/357/plan.md:10:5. `internal/effects/effects.go:33-34`: export `ErrTransient = gitx.ErrTransient` alongside the others.\n.ard/357/plan.md:11:6. `internal/committer/errors.go`: add `ErrTransient = errors.New(\"committer: transient remote failure persisted\")`, new; `lane.run` returns an error that wraps both it and the last cause, so callers can match with `errors.Is`.\n.ard/357/plan.md:13:   - Add `maxTransient = 5` and a `transientBackoff(n int) time.Duration` on `core` (new): 1s,2s,4s,8s,16s with ±25% jitter, total capped about 1 minute. Honour `cfg.Backoff` when set so tests stay fast (tests pass a zero-delay func).\n.ard/357/plan.md:14:   - In `lane.attempt` (line 404-406) return a third state. Change the `retry bool` result into a small `retryKind` (none, rejection, transient) or return the error and classify in `run` with `errors.Is(err, effects.ErrTransient)`. The latter is the smaller change: `attempt` keeps `retry=false` for transient and `run` checks the error.\n.ard/357/plan.md:15:   - In `lane.run` (line 251-291) keep two counters: `pushes` (rejections, `maxPushes`) and `transients` (`maxTransient`), independent. On a transient error from `fetch` or from `attempt`: `reset`, log `committer.retry` at `InfoContext` with `\"reason\", \"transient\"`, branch, attempt and the (scrubbed) `err`, sleep `transientBackoff`, loop again. Do not set `prev = base` for the lease-conflict check unless the push was rejected; a transient retry re-fetches, so a landed push is seen.\n.ard/357/plan.md:17:   - Exhaustion: return the error wrapping `ErrTransient` (`%w`), `Attempts` set.\n.ard/357/plan.md:20:[Omitted long matching line]\n.ard/357/plan.md:21:10. `internal/worker/run.go:628-640`: when `CommitCode` returns `committer.ErrTransient`, finish with `closeout.CausePushTransient`, transient true and `!jb.pushed` retry, instead of `CauseNoProcess` (line 641).\n.ard/357/plan.md:26:- `internal/gitx/gitx_test.go` `TestPushTransientClassification` (table): stderr `remote: Internal Server Error`, `The requested URL returned error: 502`, `Could not resolve host: github.com`, `Connection reset by peer`, `early EOF`, `RPC failed` each give `ErrTransient`; `stale info` stays `ErrStaleLease`; `non-fast-forward` stays `ErrNonFastForward`; `error: 403` is not transient. Use a fake `git` on PATH or the existing runner seam.\n.ard/357/plan.md:28:- Token failure: a `TokenFunc` returning a `*net.DNSError` gives `ErrTransient`; a plain error does not.\n.ard/357/plan.md:31:- `TestTransientExhausted`: always 500. Expect `errors.Is(err, ErrTransient)` after `maxTransient` tries, and a rejection counter that is independent (a mix of one stale lease and transients still gets its full budgets).\n.ard/357/plan.md:34:- `internal/closeout/closer_test.go`: commit returns `ErrTransient` gives `OutcomeRetry`, cause `push_transient`, no `ard:executor:failed`; a job that is itself a retry has the expected plan. A non-transient commit error still gives `failedPlan`.\n.ard/357/plan.md:36:- Edge cases: ctx cancelled during the backoff returns `ctx.Err()`, not `ErrTransient`; jitter stays within the cap.\n.ard/357/review-eng-review.md:19:      The worker branch for committer.ErrTransient (CausePushTransient, retry only when !jb.pushed) still has no test. It is the second place that maps the error to a cause, and plan.md step 10 covers it.\n.ard/357/worker-engineer.md:9:- `internal/gitx`: new `ErrTransient`; stderr classification for push and fetch (stale lease, non-fast-forward, ref-not-found and repo-access still win); token mint errors classified through `github.IsTransientToken`.\n