--k8s-instance`, `--k8s-agent-image`, `--k8s-pod-image` (both images pinned by `@sha256:` digest), `--k8s-git-base` (default `https://github.com`), `--k8s-resources` (`cpu=`, `memory=`, `memory-limit=`, `ephemeral-storage=` for the agent container), `--k8s-pre-budget` (5m) and `--k8s-result-grace` (2m). With `executor: k8s`, startup fails (exit 1) if the credential is a personal access token (also under `--dry-run`), a required flag is missing, or the config sets `roles_repo` (not supported with k8s yet). If no config has loaded and the cluster flags are set, the mode is unknown and no job loops are built until restart (`serve.executor_unresolved`). At startup the `pool-adopt` hook calls the executor's `Sweep`, which deletes this repo's job pods and Secrets that no running job record owns; pods with a record go through the Reaper's normal `Orphaned` path. The Reaper maps the executor's end reasons to causes: `evicted` (pod evicted, deleted or never scheduled; transient, one automatic retry), `clone_failed` (transient), and `no_process` for a failed prep step, bad result or missing result. Inputs over the manifest cap close out as `inputs_too_large` and are not retried. Live read tokens are added to the redaction set. `ard config check` prints a note that cluster settings come from `ard serve` flags.\n331:**Agent CLIs plug in through adapters.** Each adapter turns (prompt file, context paths, budget) into a command line and parses the exit code and, where the CLI reports them, turns and cost. For Claude Code that is `claude -p --output-format=stream-json --verbose --restricted --safe-mode --strict-mcp-config --disable-slash-commands --permission-mode=dontAsk --settings='{\"includeGitInstructions\":false,\"disableAllHooks\":true}' --tools=… --allowed-tools=… --disallowed-tools=… --model <model> --max-budget-usd <max_budget_usd> --append-system-prompt-file <role prompt> -- <message>` (`--verbose` is required by `stream-json` in print mode). Every stage (scanner, triage