{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017sceG72Dj86nfZRj3crTTf","type":"tool_result","content":"\tCostUSD *float64 `json:\",omitempty\"`\n\tSteps   int      `json:\",omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// CauseKind names why a job ended without a usable result.\ntype CauseKind string\n\n// Cause kinds. The reason in the comment is \"<kind>: <detail>\".\nconst (\n\tCauseQuiet     CauseKind = \"heartbeat_quiet\"    // no log output for 10 minutes\n\tCauseDeadline  CauseKind = \"deadline\"           // ran past its timeout\n\tCauseRestart   CauseKind = \"controller_restart\" // orphaned, gone or never started across a restart\n\tCauseNoProcess CauseKind = \"no_process\"         // never started, or its process vanished in this run\n\tCauseRateLimit CauseKind = \"rate_limit\"         // the agent reported a transient API error\n\tCauseCloneFail CauseKind = \"clone_failed\"       // a loop's Prepare failed at git or clone\n\t// CausePushTransient: a push or fetch hit a GitHub 5xx or a network error\n\t// that outlasted the committer's retries.\n\tCausePushTransient CauseKind = \"push_transient\"\n\tCauseEvicted       CauseKind = \"evicted\" // the Kubernetes pod was evicted, deleted or never scheduled\n\t// CauseInputsTooLarge: the job's untrusted inputs exceed what a pod\n\t// manifest carries. Never retried.\n\tCauseInputsTooLarge CauseKind = \"inputs_too_large\"\n\t// CauseUsageLimit: the run stopped at a subscription usage limit. It is\n\t// not a failure and never hands off to the automatic retry (Retry is\n\t// false); the issue is re-claimed after the reset.\n\tCauseUsageLimit CauseKind = \"usage_limit\"\n)\n\n// Cause is why a job ended. Detail is fixed, non-secret text.\ntype Cause struct {\n\tKind      CauseKind\n\t}\n\tc.d.log().Warn(\"closeout: commit failed\", \"job\", rec.Job.ID, \"error\", err)\n\tif p.Outcome == OutcomeRetry || p.Outcome == OutcomeLimited {\n\t\t// The log is evidence, not the result: a retry or a limit stop must\n\t\t// not turn into a failure because it could not be committed (a worker\n\t\t// that stopped before its first push has no branch to commit to).\n\t\tp.Files, p.LogPath = nil, \"\"\n\t\tp.Reason += \"; log not committed: \" + err.Error()\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\ttail, tailWithheld, keep := p.Tail, p.TailWithheld, p.KeepUntil\n\tif isReview && errors.Is(err, committer.ErrBranchGone) {\n\t\tc.prGone(rec, \"branch gone\", \"branch_gone\")\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tif errors.Is(err, committer.ErrTransient) {\n\t\t// The remote was unavailable past the committer's retries: not a\n\t\t// failure that needs a human. The job hands off to the automatic\n\t\t// retry like any named transient cause.\n\t\trec.Job.Cause = Cause{Kind: CausePushTransient, Detail: \"remote unavailable after retries\", Transient: true, Retry: true}\n\t\t*p = retryPlan(rec.Job, \"push_transient: remote unavailable after retries\")\n\t\tp.Tail, p.TailWithheld, p.KeepUntil = tail, tailWithheld, keep\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tif errors.Is(err, committer.ErrMerge) {\n\t\treturn c.commitConflict(ctx, rec, err, tail, tailWithheld, keep)\n\t}\n\t*p = failedPlan(rec.Job, \"commit failed: \"+err.Error(), p.LogWithheld)\n\tp.Tail, p.TailWithheld, p.KeepUntil = tail, tailWithheld, keep\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// prGone turns a review's plan into a stale one: its PR was merged or closed,\n// or its branch deleted, so there is nothing to commit to and nothing failed.\nfunc (c *Closer) prGone(rec *Record, why, state string) {\n\tc.d.log().Warn(\"review.pr_gone\", \"job\", rec.Job.ID, \"pr\", rec.Job.PR, \"issue\", rec.Job.Issue,\n\t\t\"role\", rec.Job.Role, \"state\", state)\n\trec.Plan = stalePRPlan(rec.Plan, rec.Job, why)\n}\n\n// commitConflict turns a plan.md merge conflict into needs-human. Like an\n\t\t}\n\t\tkind := \"push\"\n\t\tvar ge *committer.GuardError\n\t\tswitch {\n\t\tcase errors.Is(err, committer.ErrBranchExists):\n\t\t\tkind = \"branch exists\"\n\t\tcase errors.Is(err, committer.ErrConflict):\n\t\t\tkind = \"conflict\"\n\t\tcase errors.Is(err, committer.ErrBranchGone):\n\t\t\tkind = \"branch gone\"\n\t\tcase errors.As(err, &ge):\n\t\t\tkind = \"guard\"\n\t\t}\n\t\tjb.log.Error(\"worker.push_failed\", \"kind\", kind, \"error\", err)\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, committer.ErrTransient) {\n\t\t\tjb.finishWithPR(ctx, s, \"\", jb.cause(closeout.CausePushTransient, \"could not push the branch: remote unavailable after retries\", !jb.pushed))\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false\n\t\t}\n\t\tjb.finishWithPR(ctx, s, \"\", jb.cause(closeout.CauseNoProcess, \"could not push the branch: \"+kind, false))\n\t\treturn \"\", false\n\t}\n\t// The branch is on the remote from here: any failure below still opens the PR.\n\tjb.pushed = true\n\tif !jb.exists {\n\t\tjb.exists = true\n\t\tif err := d.Store.SetBranch(ctx, jb.sj.ID, jb.branch); err != nil {\n\t\t\tjb.log.Error(\"worker.set_branch_failed\", \"error\", err)\n\t\t\tjb.finishWithPR(ctx, s, \"\", jb.cause(closeout.CauseNoProcess, \"could not record the branch\", false))\n\t\t\treturn \"\", false\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tjb.log.Info(\"worker.push\", \"branch\", jb.branch, \"sha\", res.SHA, \"files\", len(req.Files), \"noop\", res.NoOp)\n\tjb.head = res.SHA\n\treturn res.SHA, true\n}\n\ninternal/closeout/closeout.go:110:\t// CausePushTransient: a push or fetch hit a GitHub 5xx or a network error\ninternal/closeout/closeout.go:112:\tCausePushTransient CauseKind = \"push_transient\"\ninternal/closeout/closeout.go:644:\t\trec.Job.Cause = Cause{Kind: CausePushTransient, Detail: \"remote unavailable after retries\", Transient: true, Retry: true}\ninternal/worker/run.go:645:\t\t\tjb.finishWithPR(ctx, s, \"\", jb.cause(closeout.CausePushTransient, \"could not push the branch: remote unavailable after retries\", !jb.pushed))\n36:        C[\"Committer: sole writer to main\"]\n138:A worker's inputs are `.ard-input/<issue#>/issue.md`, `comments.md` and, on a fix step, `test-output.log` (written by the loop, never committed) and `.ard/<\n140:Close-out checks `plan.md` against the job's base commit, but the committer writes it onto the latest `main`. So at commit time the committer replaces only \n179:**All agent output is committed too.** Each run's full output lands in `.ard/<issue#>/logs/<stage>-<role>-<ts>.log`. Close-out redacts known secret values f\n183:**One committer for main.** (Concurrency rule, #411: the clone's lock is exclusive for worktree add/remove/prune and shared for fetches, so a lane's fetch n\n185:**Why `.ard/` stays on `main` (decided, #1).** An orphan `ard-state` branch is ruled out: worker and reviewer logs ride on PR branches, and a PR cannot carr\n187:**Directories outlive their issues as the audit trail.** The janitor loop (`internal/janitor`) wakes daily but works once per 30 days (the timestamp is in m\n215:6. **File.** Edits and closes first, then joins, then new issues. Create the issue with `ard:scanner:<name>` plus the route's label (`ard:pending` by defaul\n223:**Dry-run files nothing.** Under `--dry-run` a would-be issue gets a synthetic negative number, stored in the scanner's dry-run database like a real one, so\n273:5. Close out: read `triage-<role>.md` frontmatter, send the issue directory (and nothing else) to the committer, post the summary as a comment, swap `:runni\n279:The starter lead (`.ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt`) follows a fixed contract. It reads the issue only through the untrusted input files `.ard-input/<issue#>/is\n281:The starter engineer (`.ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt`) plans for the worker without implementing. Its inputs are `.ard-input/<issue#>/issue.md`, `comments\n308:Local-executor details: the role directory (and its `Dockerfile`) is mounted from the config snapshot at the job's SHA, not from the working tree. The job w\n331:**Agent CLIs plug in through adapters.** Each adapter turns (prompt file, context paths, budget) into a command line and parses the exit code and, where the\n358:3. **Steps.** One worker job is one state row, one pool slot and one attempt, but it ru