{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015iBedMQ6KBmQ45x991S3vt","type":"tool_result","content":"**One committer for main.** (Concurrency rule, #411: the clone's lock is exclusive for worktree add/remove/prune and shared for fetches, so a lane's fetch never reads a half-added or half-removed worktree; commits and pushes take neither.) Close-outs never push. They hand a file set to the controller's committer, which keeps its own clean worktree of `main`, commits as `ard[bot]` with `ard(<stage>:<role>): #<issue> <summary> [skip ci]`, re-applies its snapshot on the fetched head, pushes with a lease, and retries up to 3 times (re-applying the whole-file snapshot is the rebase; if upstream changed one of its paths the request fails with a conflict instead of overwriting). A replay of an unchanged tree is a no-op that returns the upstream head. It refuses any change outside the `.ard/<issue#>/` directories. Worker code takes a separate lane: `Branches.CommitCode` commits only paths `committer.CheckCodePath` accepts (nothing under `.ard/`, `.ard-input/` or `.github/`, no `.git` or secret-shaped names), only to `worker/` branches, creating a branch with a push whose lease expects it to be absent and refusing to overwrite a path that changed on the branch since the job started. The one other lane is `ard init --pr`'s (local mode writes only the working tree, #303): it commits only `.ard/config.yaml`, `.ard/ard-init.lock` and files under the four role trees, only to the new branch `ard-init` cut from `main`, with a push whose lease expects the ref to be absent, so it creates the branch and never updates an existing one, and opens a PR; a human merges it with a squash or merge commit, so the bot-commit check never sees a bot commit outside `.ard/<issue#>/` on main's first-parent history. Because the bot must bypass branch protection on `main`, a detective check audits it: the workflow `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` walks the first-parent history of `main` (the last 500 commits, or everything after the repository variable `ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE`) and fails the run, listing the commits and paths in the job summary, when a commit made by the bot changes anything but regular files under a single `.ard/<issue#>/` directory. Bot commits are identified by **committer** (the App's noreply email or login), not author, because a squash merge of a bot PR has the bot as author. If the 500-commit window is full and its oldest commit is the bot's, the check fails closed until `ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE` is set, so a bad commit cannot be flushed out of view. It runs hourly as well as on push, because `[skip ci]` suppresses the push trigger. It fails closed when the `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` repository variable is unset. It reads both variables from repository settings and lives in `.github/workflows/`, which the App cannot write. Alerting is the failed run only; it does not open issues or pause ard.\ninternal/closeout/closeout.go:652:\t*p = failedPlan(rec.Job, \"commit failed: \"+err.Error(), p.LogWithheld)\ninternal/closeout/plan.go:196:// failedPlan is the plan for a job that did not produce a usable result.\ninternal/closeout/plan.go:197:func failedPlan(j Job, reason string, logWithheld bool) Plan {\ninternal/closeout/prepare.go:239:\t\tplan = failedPlan(j, cleanReason(ctx, red, failed), logWithheld)\ninternal/committer/committer_test.go:47:func (e *env) live() *effects.Live {\ninternal/committer/committer_test.go:51:func (e *env) main(t *testing.T, fx Effects) *Committer {\ninternal/committer/committer_test.go:61:func (e *env) head(t *testing.T, ref string) string {\ninternal/committer/init_test.go:58:func (e *env) init(t *testing.T, fx Effects) *Init {\ninternal/committer/init_test.go:67:func (e *env) hasBranch(t *testing.T, name string) bool {\n33:\tErrNonFastForward  = gitx.ErrNonFastForward\n65:func isNothing(err error) bool { return errors.Is(err, ErrNothingToCommit) }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessio